            <zone h='33921' id='5' paired-zone-id='4' removable='false' type-v2='flipboard' w='98426' x='787' y='65249'>
              <flipboard active-id='1' nav-type='caption' show-nav-arrows='true'>
                <story-points>
                  <story-point caption='Medals by Country: Global Olympic Sports Performance Analysis&#10;&#10;This visualization presents a comparative analysis of Olympic medal-winning records across different countries, highlighting variations in their performance throughout the Olympic Games. The primary objective of this analysis is to identify leading countries and examine the distribution of Gold, Silver, and Bronze medal records.&#10;&#10;The horizontal stacked bar chart represents each country&apos;s medal-winning records, with the length of each bar indicating the number of distinct athlete IDs associated with medal-winning performances. The different colours distinguish the three medal categories: Gold, Silver, and Bronze. This arrangement makes it easier to compare countries based on their overall records and examine the contribution of each medal category to their performance.&#10;&#10;The visualization provides a clear overview of the differences in Olympic achievements among participating countries. Countries with longer bars have higher counts of medal-winning athlete records in the selected dataset, while the coloured segments help illustrate how these records are distributed across the three medal categories. The chart also allows viewers to identify countries with comparatively strong gold-medal records and those with a more balanced distribution of medal types.&#10;&#10;Furthermore, this comparison demonstrates how data visualization can transform a large collection of Olympic records into an understandable visual summary. It supports the exploration of international sporting performance and helps identify patterns that may be investigated further using other charts in the project, such as medal distribution, athlete participation by year, and comparisons between Summer and Winter Olympics.&#10;&#10;Key Objective: To compare medal-winning records across countries, understand the distribution of Gold, Silver, and Bronze records, and identify differences in Olympic performance using the available dataset.&#10;&#10;Analytical Insight: The United States (USA) has the longest bar in the displayed view, indicating the highest count of distinct athlete IDs associated with medal-winning records among the countries shown. Other countries can be compared using both their overall bar lengths and the relative sizes of their medal-category segments.&#10;&#10;Conclusion: This visualization provides a foundation for understanding global Olympic performance. By comparing countries and their medal-category records, it helps viewers explore differences in sporting achievements and establishes a starting point for more detailed analysis of Olympic medal trends.' captured-sheet='01 medal by country' id='1' />
                </story-points>
              </flipboard>
            </zone>
          </zone>
          <zone-style>
